{#
  Grafana's dashboards, ONE ConfigMap per `observability_dashboard_folders` entry, each holding
  that folder's boards under their file names. grafana.yaml.j2 mounts each one at
  /var/lib/grafana/dashboards/homelab/<folder>.

  Rendered here rather than staged on the node and built by a task (D5's imperative-ConfigMap
  row), so the ConfigMaps are a render that Flux can apply once observability is flux-owned.
  Each board passes through `grafana_deploy_annotated`
  (ansible/filter_plugins/grafana_dashboards.py), which adds the two deploy-annotation queries
  and writes the JSON with sorted keys, so an unchanged board renders the same bytes.

  `manifests_exclude_files` keeps this file out of the shared role's client-side apply, which
  copies each object into a `last-applied-configuration` annotation capped at 262144 bytes.
  The Infrastructure folder is about 600 KB as JSON, so `tasks/dashboards.yml` renders it to
  its own directory and applies it server-side, which writes no such annotation. The flip PR
  drops the exclusion: Flux applies server-side too, and the file then renders into the
  `observability` bundle. ansible/tests/services/test_dashboard_configmaps.py holds every
  ConfigMap under the 1 MiB object cap.

  `lookup('file')` strips trailing whitespace, which the JSON parse ignores. The `|` block keeps
  exactly one trailing newline, so each key equals the filter's output byte for byte.

  Keep comments at column 0 and above the documents: an indented comment between two keys would
  land inside the preceding block scalar.
#}
{% for folder, boards in observability_dashboard_folders | dictsort %}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: grafana-dashboards-{{ folder | lower }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_observability_namespace }}
data:
{% for board in boards %}
  {{ board }}: |
{{ lookup('file', playbook_dir ~ '/roles/k8s/observability/files/dashboards/' ~ folder ~ '/' ~ board) | grafana_deploy_annotated(observability_loki_homelab_uid, observability_deploy_annotation_expr, observability_flux_deploy_annotation_expr) | indent(4, true) }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
